 "interpretation": "The rule resolves a contrast when its point estimate is >= the MDE AND the lower bound is > 0; since lower = point - distance, that needs point > 0.0086 STRICTLY, as well as >= 0.0056. The registered MDE is BELOW the distance, so a contrast landing at the MDE cannot resolve. The mandate records the EXPECTATION that a distance measured between unrelated models over-estimates a same-init contrast's width; that is an expectation about correlated per-query differences, not a guarantee -- paired variance can move either way -- and it is recorded, not corrected. The sensitivity row prices it as arithmetic."
